  "ourearth-zimbabwe": {"t":"Who built Great Zimbabwe, and why was the answer buried? (search excerpt; not read in full): built by Bantu-speaking ancestors of the Shona c. 1100-1450; Mauch in 1871, Bent in 1891, Randall-MacIver in 1905 and Caton-Thompson in 1929; the Rhodesian government censored the finding from 1965 to 1980","s":"Our Earth's History","d":"14/11/2026","u":"https://ourearthshistory.com/africa/medieval/who-built-great-zimbabwe/"},
  "sciam-zimbabwe": {"t":"Great Zimbabwe (Scientific American, 2005; search excerpt): Mauch concluded in 1871 that the ruins were not African work; Bent in 1891 dug round the conical tower; Randall-MacIver in 1905 concluded that Africans built it; Caton-Thompson agreed in 1929","s":"Scientific American","d":"14/11/2026","u":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/great-zimbabwe-2005-01/"},
  "iccrom-zimbabwe": {"t":"The Preservation of Great Zimbabwe (ICCROM, 2009; search excerpt): the settler community rejected Randall-MacIver's findings; Scholfield in 1926 and Caton-Thompson in 1929 concluded that the structures were of African authorship","s":"ICCROM","d":"14/11/2026","u":"https://www.iccrom.org/sites/default/files/publications/2019-11/iccrom_ics04_zimbabwe_en.pdf"},
